// octonarium -- the driver half of the lane-parallel triangle.
//
// The pictura/triangulum arrangement: octonaria.exsc's rasterizer is
// pure arithmetic; this file is where authority enters, once, as the
// `Mundus` parameter (§4.1 rule 2), handing the renderer the
// standard-output writer and checking its byte count. The program's
// syscall surface is write(1) and exit_group.
//
// The image's 1555215 bytes are decided before any of them is written:
// the computation is fixed-order f32 arithmetic under nearest-even, so
// the differential phase over gcc/clang at -O0/-O2, the big-endian
// mips64 cross run (the lane bytes are written through explicit
// scribe_octeto calls, never a memory image), and the numpy oracle
// (prototypes/pictura_octonaria_oracle.py) all reproduce it.

publica functio initium(m: Mundus) -> u8 {
    firma a = m.ambitus();
    sub ambitus = a;
    firma s = Scriptor.ad_exitum(a);
    firma n = scribe_octonaria(s);
    si n ne 1555215 {
        redde 1;
    }
    redde 0;
}
